                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="455886" author="adilger" created="Tue, 13 May 2025 23:32:35 +0000"  >&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Overall these values are definet as if they are the bits in a bitmask, but are never used as such which makes everything super confusing, so probably ripe for some rework?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
#define LU_SEQ_RANGE_MDT        0x0
#define LU_SEQ_RANGE_OST        0x1
#define LU_SEQ_RANGE_ANY        0x3
#define LU_SEQ_RANGE_MASK       0x3
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These constants are in &lt;tt&gt;lustre_idl.h&lt;/tt&gt; so they form part of the on-disk format and/or network protocol, so they cannot just be changed.  It looks like the check should be changed to use the existing helper functions that implement this correctly (which I found after I had proposed an almost identical helper function to implement this check):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
                &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (fld_range_is_mdt(&amp;amp;u.range))
                        err = u.range.lsr_index;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="455887" author="adilger" created="Tue, 13 May 2025 23:36:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Note, it appears that this is the only similar misuse of &lt;tt&gt;LU_SEQ_RANGE_MDT&lt;/tt&gt; as a mask.  All other users either set or check equivalence to either &lt;tt&gt;LU_SEQ_RANGE_MDT&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;LU_SEQ_RANGE_OST&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="455898" author="green" created="Wed, 14 May 2025 01:40:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;yes, misuse is just one place, but it&apos;s facilitated by very unfortunate and confusing naming of these defines and surrounding functions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So we have to address that as well or more similar breakage would appear.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;E.g. I think the whole &quot;MASK&quot; thing could be removed and all users revisited&quot;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="455900" author="green" created="Wed, 14 May 2025 02:14:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;soundslike the only user of the _MASK is fld_range_type&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And the only user of fld_range_type outside of fld_range_is_xxx is fld_local_lookup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wonder what stops us from dropping fld_range_type completely and replace it with just using hte range value directly in all cases?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494634" author="JIRAUSER19573" created="Sat, 16 May 2026 20:05:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Oleg - I happened to look at this and thinking if we drop the fld_range_type() and thus also LU_SEQ_RANGE_MASK then we will compare range-&amp;gt;lsr_flags directly with the assumption that it will always have bits that are defined in the types (I do see everywhere else, the code is actually doing that)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Or &lt;br/&gt;
we fix the comparison in server_ioctl()&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
               err = obd_get_info(env, lsi-&amp;gt;lsi_osd_exp, sizeof(KEY_FID2IDX),
 &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;KEY_FID2IDX, &amp;amp;len, &amp;amp;u.fid);
 &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (err == 0) {
 &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; err = -EINVAL;
 &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; ((u.range.lsr_flags &amp;amp; LU_SEQ_RANGE_MASK) == LU_SEQ_RANGE_MDT) &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;
                                err = u.range.lsr_index;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and also fix fld_range_set_type() along with other places in the code where assumption is that lsr_flags would always have only the bits that are defined&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; inline void fld_range_set_type(struct lu_seq_range *range, unsigned flags)
{    
     range-&amp;gt;lsr_flags &amp;amp;= ~LU_SEQ_RANGE_MASK;
     range-&amp;gt;lsr_flags |= flags &amp;amp; LU_SEQ_RANGE_MASK;
} &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494691" author="green" created="Sun, 17 May 2026 06:44:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I have no strong opinion and suspect we should drop the MASK and go to comparisons.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Was hoping to get a bit of a comment from &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=bzzz&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;bzzz&quot;&gt;bzzz&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494704" author="bzzz" created="Mon, 18 May 2026 07:46:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;fld_range_is_mdt(&amp;amp;u.range) looks clear, short and self-explaining to me.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494820" author="gerrit" created="Wed, 20 May 2026 23:30:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Sonia Sharma &amp;lt;sonia.sh.sharma@oracle.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66042&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66042&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
